  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...No significant weather concerns this week.\n\nHigh pressure centered over New England will build east and then move\noffshore tonight. A weak cold front passes through the region Friday,\nand then high pressure returns for the weekend. Low pressure may\napproach the region for the start of next week.\n\nWith high pressure remaining north/northeast of the area today,\nwe expect another sunny and dry day. High temps will range from\nthe upper 50s/low 60s across the far N/W areas to the mid/upper\n60s elsewhere. These temps a bit above normal for Oct. 28.\n\nAfter that, dry conditions through Saturday with high temperatures\ngenerally from the mid and upper 60s on Wednesday to the mid \n70s or so by Friday. Cooler, but still slightly above normal \ntemperatures expected for this weekend. Rain may arrive on \nSunday or Monday depending on the timing, strength, and \nplacement of that aforementioned low pressure system.",
